      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, that\u0027s what I was expecting. Thinking about this a bit more though I\u0027m not sure if that will behave correctly with a **static node** that has subnodes.\n\nIt looks like we\u0027d transition the main node from `SLOT_HOST` to `FAILED` here. The static provider would then cycle it to `REBUILDING`.\n\nAs long as the main node is in state `FAILED` we\u0027d raise an exception in line 2430 above. When the main node is e.g. `REBUILDING`, we will change the main node back to failed in case the nodescan for the subnode still fails.\n\nIt looks like we might converge back to the correct state after the node is available again. But considering the above behavior this feels more like a happy accident.\n\nI think we should probably create a test and validate those assumptions.",
      "parentUuid": "2737fba9_7fdb4f6a",
      "revId": "cafd6f7e6a00b97111a3ce132caa36f3897599b4",
